{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"nl -ba DESIGN.md && nl -ba packages/contracts/src/interfaces/IRaffle.sol | sed -n '152,190p' && nl -ba packages/contracts/node_modules/@chainlink/contracts/src/v0.8/vrf/dev/VRFV2PlusWrapperConsumerBase.sol | sed -n '140,190p'\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t# Clean design specification\n     2\tEthereum NFT raffle; immutable factory, ERC-1167 clones with immutable implementation. One entry costs 1,000,000 units of canonical six-decimal USDC. One purchase mints a transferable ERC721 ticket representing a contiguous inclusive range. Exactly one ERC721 prize is escrowed atomically at creation. Reserve met awards NFT and 95% sponsor / 5% treasury. Reserve missed awards 80% gross to winner, 15% sponsor, 5% treasury. Refund outcome pays 100% per entry and returns prize. Rounding is floor on aggregate protocol fee; remainder must be allocated without loss. No administrator, mutable configuration or upgrade. Request window [sale end, end+2days); callback accepted strictly before request timestamp+2days. Refunds open at deadline. Callback records result only. Settlement is permissionless, storage-only; redemption requires current ticket owner, burns claim atomically, and must revert all effects on delivery failure. Sponsor and treasury can claim independently after settlement. Never move assets between raffle clones. Quote token and Chainlink wrapper are trusted canonical dependencies; arbitrary prize contracts and ticket recipients are untrusted. Frontend discovery is advisory; transaction decisions must reread current chain state.\n     3\t\n     4\tThis specification was composed before scanner results and historical findings. Source, not design prose, determines actual behavior. No tests, audit history, accepted-risk lists or scanner results are provided.\n   152\t    /// @param remainingRefundLiability Raw six-decimal quote-token units still claimable after this refund.\n   153\t    event TicketsRefunded(\n   154\t        address indexed owner,\n   155\t        uint256 ticketQuantity,\n   156\t        uint256 entryQuantity,\n   157\t        uint256 amount,\n   158\t        uint256 remainingRefundLiability\n   159\t    );\n   160\t\n   161\t    /// @notice Emitted when the complete current sponsor balance is released to its immutable recipient.\n   162\t    /// @param caller Address that triggered the permissionless release.\n   163\t    /// @param recipient Immutable sponsor recipient that received the payment.\n   164\t    /// @param amount Raw six-decimal quote-token units paid.\n   165\t    event SponsorProceedsReleased(address indexed caller, address indexed recipient, uint256 amount);\n   166\t\n   167\t    /// @notice Emitted when the complete current protocol-fee balance is released to the immutable treasury.\n   168\t    /// @param caller Address that triggered the permissionless release.\n   169\t    /// @param treasury Immutable protocol treasury that received the payment.\n   170\t    /// @param amount Raw six-decimal quote-token units paid.\n   171\t    event ProtocolFeesReleased(address indexed caller, address indexed treasury, uint256 amount);\n   172\t\n   173\t    /// @notice Emitted when the escrowed prize is returned after a cash result or refund transition.\n   174\t    /// @param caller Address that triggered the permissionless release.\n   175\t    /// @param recipient Immutable sponsor recipient that received the prize.\n   176\t    /// @param prizeToken ERC-721 contract of the returned prize.\n   177\t    /// @param prizeTokenId Token ID of the returned prize.\n   178\t    event SponsorPrizeReleased(\n   179\t        address indexed caller, address indexed recipient, address indexed prizeToken, uint256 prizeTokenId\n   180\t    );\n   181\t\n   182\t    // Errors\n   183\t\n   184\t    /// @notice Raised when a caller other than the immutable factory attempts clone initialization.\n   185\t    error OnlyFactory();\n   186\t\n   187\t    /// @notice Raised when initialization is attempted more than once or on the locked implementation.\n   188\t    error AlreadyInitialized();\n   189\t\n   190\t    /// @notice Raised when a required address is the zero address.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
